					<u>Ag.</u>
					572
				</span></i>
			 (nisi leg.<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ξυμφοράς</span>)
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">; φράσαι . . χαίρειν Ἀθηναίοισι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Nu.</u>
					609
				</span></i>
			 (troch.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολλὰ εἰπόντα χ. τῷ ἀληθεῖ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Phdr.</u>
					272e
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Phd.</u>
				64c
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>R.</u>
				406d
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>HG</u>
				4.1.31
			</span></i> (codd., fort. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλλήλους</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Jul.
			</span></i><i>ad Them.</i><i><span class="en">
				255a
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> on other
			occasions, as in comforting, <i>be of good cheer,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Od.
				8.408
			</span></i>; at meals, <i><span class="en">
				4.60
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				18.122
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χαῖρε, γύναι, φιλότητι</span>
			<i>good luck be</i> on our union, <i><span class="en">
				11.248
			</span></i>; 
