					186
				</span></i>
			; cf. supr. <i><span class="en">
				11
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> in the same
			sense as imper. (supr. <i><span class="en">
				111
			</span></i>), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σὺ δέ μοι χαίρων ἀφίκοιο</span>
			<i>fare</i>-thee-<i>well,</i> and may'st thou arrive, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				15.128
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				2.163
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χαίροισ᾽ ἔρχεο</span> go thy
			way <i>rejoicing,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Sapph.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				23.7
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλλ᾽ ἑρπέτω χαίρουσα</span>
			let her go <i>with a benison,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Tr.</u>
				819
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χαίρων ἴθι</span>
			<i>fare</i>-thee-<i>well,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Alc.</u>
				813
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ph.</u>
